## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about cross-tenant data isolation, token binding, and incident response in a realistic multi-tenant platform similar to large-scale chat/workspace products.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege per-automation scopes
- Token binding to tenant identity and audience (aud/iss)
- Short-lived tokens with rapid rotation
- Per-resource RBAC/ACL enforcement
- API gateway policy checks and runtime validation
- Tamper-evident audit logs and a 24h IR playbook

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation: verify JWT claims for a request
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authorize(token, requiredScope, tenantId) {
  const payload = jwt.verify(token, PUBLIC_KEY, { algorithms:['RS256'] });
  if (payload.aud !== 'automation') return false;
  if (payload.tenant !== tenantId) return false;
  if (!payload.scopes.includes(requiredScope)) return false;
  // ensure token is recent
  return true;
}
```

